-- Double I-selection (NOTES §5): s I I V NEXT; V's argument is the second tag on a
-- zero stream and NEXT on a variable; NEXT plays the variable arm. ABS/APP each bind
-- and erase the trailing NEXT and each holds its own parse. Expected well above 162.
(\x. x x) (\x. (\intL. \cont. \list.
  list (\a. a) (\a. a)
    (\u. u
      (\r2 \n. intL (\exp. cont (\args \arg. exp (\zx \zy. zx arg (zy args)))) r2)
      (\r2 \n. intL (\exp. intL (\exp2. cont (\args. exp args (exp2 args)))) r2))
    (\a \p. list (\q. cont) (list list a)))
  (x x))
